    "MAU is an INPUT, not an out-of-sample check: flag persistence p(tau) is fitted against it and the tail kernel is solved from it. DAU cannot identify the tail kernel -- arrivals are inverted from DAU and absorb any change to it -- so MAU is what pins it, at 4.94 active days.",
    "The tail kernel's SHAPE is borrowed from the last measurable cohort; only its scale is solved. A cohort's behaviour is unknowable until it has lived 28 days, so every projection assumes one.",
    "The plateau is a planning assumption, not an estimate. No inflection has been observed, so the ceiling is not identifiable from the data.",
    "The `age <= 28d` clause can only see automation younger than four weeks. It is safe today because the 28-180d band is flat; if that band rises the component is under-counted. Monitored on the evidence page."
